# APML: Structure tree — row grammar + demo-refresh verb
# Last updated: 2026-07-20
# Contracts: docs/THE-MODEL.md §1.9/§1.12, docs/THE-VIEW.md §2; founder rulings
# 2026-07-19 (rows are links; ⋯ maintenance-only) + 2026-07-20 (quiet chips,
# hierarchy rails); refresh demo data as a verb on a DEMO node

purpose: |
  The Structure page (/admin/structure) is the org tree's editing surface —
  two lenses (tree/table) over the same group nodes. This spec pins the ROW
  GRAMMAR (how a row's verbs are laid out) and the demo-refresh verb.

ordering: |
  Both lenses (tree + table) list groups/schools alphabetical by name —
  api/groups/tree.ts and api/groups/table.ts, via api/_utils/alphaSort.ts;
  StructureTreeNode.vue sorts its visible children the same way client-side.
  The legacy GroupTreeNode.vue (Demos tool only — see structure-tree's
  sibling doc for demo orgs) matches this too as of the 2026-07-30 sibling-
  ordering pass (packages/player-vue/src/utils/alphaSort.ts) — it used to
  render children/schools in raw fetch order.

row_grammar:  # founder-ruled 2026-07-19/20 — name is the anchor, repetition is noise
  rows_are_links: |
    A click ANYWHERE on a row (tree or table lens) opens the node's HOME
    (/admin/groups/:id, or /admin/schools/:id for a commercial node) —
    THE-VIEW §2. No separate Open control; in-row controls stop propagation.
  quiet_chips:  # founder-ruled 2026-07-20 — info that repeats on every row is not info
    label_word: |
      shown ONLY where it disambiguates — when the row's own sibling set
      mixes labels (parent computes over ALL its children; AdminStructure
      does the same across roots). 10.5px faded mono when shown. Change
      label via ⋯ works regardless.
    demo_badge: marked ONCE at the demo subtree's root; descendants silent
      (parentIsDemo prop). Standalone demo roots keep theirs.
    status_pill: attention states only (trial/past_due); paid-and-fine
      silent; trial ALSO hidden for demo nodes and inside demo subtrees —
      a demo school on trial is normal state, not attention.
    size: one muted right-aligned "N learners"; full breakdown on hover.
  hierarchy:  # founder-ruled 2026-07-20 — depth legible at a glance
    rails: one faint 1px vertical guide per ancestor level (.rail, 22px
      step, 16px under 768px), stretched through row padding so lines read
      continuous; rows are flat DOM siblings so rail count IS the depth.
    typography: name steps down by level — depth-0 15px semibold,
      depth-1 14px medium, depth-2+ 13px medium. Roots anchor the page.
  overflow: |
    Maintenance verbs only, ONE always-visible ⋯ menu with labeled words:
    Rename · Change label · Delete. Create/invite/mint live on the node
    home's action bar (NodeActionBar), not on rows.
  table_lens: whole-row link + zebra stripe (rgba(44,38,34,0.03) even rows);
    rename/delete stay as row icons; label/Demo/status stay plain columns

demo_refresh:  # the verb on a DEMO node (founder-ruled 2026-07-19)
  verb: |
    "Refresh demo activity" in NodePanel, rendered ONLY when node.is_demo.
    Regenerates the node's subtree's synthetic telemetry up to the minute so
    demo dashboards never read burst-then-dead. Reports counts inline.
  endpoint: POST /api/groups/:id/demo-refresh   # api/groups/[id]/demo-refresh.ts
  engine: api/_utils/demoNodeRefresh.ts (refreshDemoNodeActivity)
  semantics:
    - REPLACE not top-up: deletes the subtree's synthetic student telemetry
      (sessions, seed_progress, lego_progress, class_sessions) then
      regenerates — idempotent, refreshes never stack
    - ~8 weeks of practice sessions, power-law weighted toward recent days
      and today; fast/steady/idle personas (20/50/30) per learner
    - per (learner, CLASS) pair, not per learner (2026-07-20): a dual-course
      learner (two class tags) gets coherent telemetry in BOTH courses, each
      anchored to its OWN enrollment cursor; personas draw per pair (fast in
      French, idle in Spanish is honest); learnersTouched counts distinct
      learners
    - positions anchored to each learner's existing enrollment cursor
      (continuing cohort, never teleported); capped by the course seed count
    - class_sessions form an ADVANCING start→end LEGO arc ending at the
      class's current_seed with the newest session today — the school/class
      rate-of-progress reads these ordinals, a fixed range rolls to zero
  hard_safety:  # impossible to touch non-demo data; server-side, refuse not skip
    - the target group row must be is_demo=true → else 403 refused
    - every school in the subtree must be is_demo=true → else refused
    - only is_demo=true learners enter the write set; STUDENT class-tags only
      (demo staff are real logins — their practice history is never touched)
    - admin-gated (verifyAdmin) + service-role writes; audit to player_events
  legacy: |
    api/_utils/demoSchoolRefresh.ts (demo_orgs-keyed, continuation top-up)
    remains for pre-2026-07-17 orgs via /api/admin/demo-schools refresh.

components:
  - packages/player-vue/src/views/admin/AdminStructure.vue
  - packages/player-vue/src/components/admin/StructureTreeNode.vue
  - packages/player-vue/src/components/admin/NodePanel.vue

tests:
  - packages/player-vue/src/components/admin/StructureTreeNode.test.ts  # Open pill; overflow words
  - packages/player-vue/src/components/admin/NodePanel.test.ts          # demo-only verb; POST + counts
  - api/_utils/demoNodeRefresh.test.ts                                  # all three safety guards; replace; arc
  - packages/player-vue/e2e/the-view/demo-refresh-walk.mjs              # deployed-dev walk (evidence in docs/the-view/demo-refresh/)
